in 2017 tom hall and spider-man swung  his way into our hearts  and so did the latest mj zendaya yeah  from mary jane to michelle jones there's  a long legacy to live up to but we think  zendaya takes the crown for the best  mj in spider-man history thank you  mj is a love interest for spidey like  we've never seen before  and with three different live-action  versions of the wall crawler  we've seen plenty somehow despite  spider-man being so frequently adapted  and rebooted  michelle jones ended up being a fresh  and innovative character  i'm messing with you let us know if you  agree with us by the end of the video  or tell us why you feel differently in  the comments you ready  yeah you're gonna love this  in a way the different spider-man  franchises provide an interesting lens  through which we can see the evolution  of women's roles in superhero movies  over the past couple of decades  we've come a long way since kristen  dunst mary jane in the original sam  raimi trilogy  while 2002 may not seem like that long  ago women's roles in superhero movies  and  action movies in general have changed so  much for the better that raymie's mj  doesn't really hold up to modern  standards for a female character  this mj may have the iconic kiss but  apart from that  and the fact that dunst rocks that red  hair there's not much else going for  this particular version of mary jane  constantly kidnapped and somehow always  finding herself in the bad guy's line of  fire  a good chunk of dunce dialogue is just  screaming for help  when she isn't in danger for the sake of  the plot her only job is to have a  complicated love life  her on-again off-again relationship with  peter parker and multiple love triangles  have her going in circles leaving little  room for her to grow as a character  while it's nice to see that mary jane  doesn't spend her time apart from peter  pining for him  instead she does her best to try and  move on nearly all of her  characterization is defined by her  relationships with men  to be fair there were efforts made to  add depth to this version of mary jane  it's just that they all fell short there  was some focus placed on her career as a  model and hopeful stage actress but it  was mostly used to contextualize peter's  feelings  adding in a backstory of her coming from  a broken home doesn't do much to flesh  out her personality  hardly ever coming into play and only  serving to play further into her role as  a helpless victim for spidey to save we  can hardly blame dunst  who gave the best performance she could  and to her credit  added charm to the character but she was  working with a script that gave her very  little to work with  the sam raimi trilogy certainly didn't  do justice to the mary jane fans who  fell in love with her in the original  comics  that's what made gwen stacy from the  amazing spider-man movies such a breath  of fresh air  well i guess i don't need to tell you  what happens if you forget that  as the romantic lead she fulfills the  same role as mj  so we decided to include her as an  honorable mention plus in the comics  she was peter's girl long before mary  jane entered his life played by emma  stone  this leading lady was a huge step in the  right direction and helped pave the way  for zendaya's mj  gwen is an assertive science genius who  plays an active role in both amazing  spider-man movies  providing the scientific solutions to  spider-man's problems  and fending for herself in the face of  danger heroic in her own right  she selflessly remains in a dangerous  area to help evacuate other civilians  proving herself to be a quick thinker  and resourceful she uses her scientific  know-how to ambush the lizard from her  hiding place with an improvised  flamethrower  despite her young age and the challenges  women face in the field of science  gwen is highly motivated and ambitious  she worked as an intern at oscorp and  graduated high school as class  valedictorian  she is even a candidate for a  scholarship to the prestigious  university of oxford  oxford i didn't know yeah stone brought  a confident yet approachable heir to the  character with her performance  full of personality from moment to  moment with an endearing quality to her  oh  she has great chemistry with andrew  garfield's peter parker  making for a downright adorable movie  couple the two seem to have a genuine  spark between them  creating an on-screen romance we loved  watching unfold  their relationship isn't always smooth  sailing but despite  all of their ups and downs gwen is there  when peter needs her most  coming to his aid when he is in over his  head and refusing to sit on the  sidelines  sadly gwen's proactive role is what  leads to her downfall  leaving spidey heartbroken in the  process this decision faced criticism as  an example of fridging a practice of  injuring or killing female characters  solely for the development or motivation  of a male character  while gwen's death was a story point  lifted directly from the original comics  some argue the modern retelling could  have and should have deviated from the  dated source material  as many felt that gwen was one of the  strong points of the amazing spider-man  reboot  comic books have had a bad reputation  for fridging given the long history of  comics  there are many once traditional details  in the canon that have since been phased  out due to changing tastes and societal  values  but fridging has remained consistent  enough to see several examples across  the cinematic adaptations of marvel  properties  although this was far from the only  problems that critics and audiences had  with the amazing spider-man 2  the film might have benefited from  defying this particular expectation  set by the source material  perhaps the decision to write an  entirely new character to play the love  interest of tom holland's peter parker  was born of a desire to break away from  the decades-old comic book story lines  michelle jones nicknamed mj is less of a  reimagining of mary  jane than her own entirely new character  marvel studios president kevin feige  expressed that the decision to give her  the initials mj was merely an homage to  spider-man's most iconic sweetheart  feige was sure to emphasize that  michelle jones is not mary jane with a  twist  making her the first on-screen romance  for peter that didn't come from the  comic books  even liz toombs in homecoming was based  on liz allen from the comics  liz was also played by a woman of color  laura harrier  despite her comic book counterpart being  a blonde white woman  regardless this casting decision didn't  come without its share of confusion  and controversy with some fans taking to  twitter in response to rumors before the  film's release that zendaya would be  playing mary jane  objecting to a traditionally white  redhead character being played by a  woman of color  this was so early on in production that  before he had even been given the chance  to read the script  director james gunn responded to the  controversy on his facebook page saying  if we're going to continue to make  movies based on the almost all white  heroes and supporting characters from  the comics of the last century  we're going to have to get used to them  being more reflective of our diverse  present world  since then the response to zendaya's mj  has been mostly positive  with critics and audiences praising the  casting decision as a much needed  injection of diversity in the mcu  while providing a fuller more  well-rounded character for peter  parker's high school sweetheart  zendaya threw herself into the role with  enthusiasm even taking inspiration from  the classic comic book icon and dyeing  her hair  red she showed off her new do by posting  a picture on her instagram with the  caption  faceit tiger a reference to mary jane's  first appearance in the comics  this was a move that showed zendaya  truly has an appreciation for the source  material  she stated in an interview with good  morning america that she went to see  spider-man on her first date when she  was just 16 and was obsessed with it  immediately  it's always a plus to see actors that  feel a personal connection with their  projects  zendaya's dedication is evident in her  performance and it's easy to tell that  she has fun with the role  her mj is the closest to a real high  schooler love interest in a spider-man  movie that there has ever been  mj feels like a truly modern update  she's sarcastic and aloof  keeping her guard up when it comes to  her feelings just like a real teenager  so where do you want to go who cares  rather than retreading the tired trope  of the hopeless nerd pining after the  unattainable popular girl  mj is already in peter's social circle  as a highly intellectual smart-mouthed  outcast  a choice that makes her far more  relatable and a bit of a rebel  beneath her cool as ice exterior she is  still a quirky young woman struggling  with ego and insecurity like any other  teen  weird although she is a member of the  academic decathlon team alongside peter  mj is more than just book smart she is  clever  and observant suspecting early on that  peter parker is spider-man's secret  identity  she's so invested in proving her theory  that it's her top priority  as opposed to peter who spent the  entirety of far from home up to that  point  obsessing over his plans to confess his  feelings to her  once her suspicions are confirmed she is  supportive  you're going to need this helping  spider-man's investigation and letting  down her walls enough to let peter into  her life as  more than a friend what really sells the  relationship is zendaya  and holland's performances giving the  couple a realistically awkward but sweet  dynamic that feels natural and true to  real life high school romances  make no mistake zendaya's mj is no shy  helpless bookworm  when she finds herself in danger she  doesn't hesitate to defend herself  taking more charge of the situation than  her teacher the actual adult in the room  thanks to her resourcefulness and her  will to take action she and the other  students managed to hold off the  villain's drones long enough to survive  until spider-man is able to deactivate  them  mj finds a good balance between throwing  herself into danger  and being a mere cheerleader on the  sidelines playing a supportive role that  lets her add to the story as an active  participant  hopefully we can look forward to her  inquisitive nature and investigative  skills  helping out peter in future installments  giving her a similar role to peter's  best friend and guy in the chair  ned judging from the ending of far from  home  spidey's certainly going to need all the  help he can get  what really sets michelle apart from the  previous is that unlike mary jane  the beautiful girl next door who becomes  a model and gwen stacy  a super genius science whiz that  graduates top of her class  mj is relatively normal she's gifted  she's smart  but she isn't held to the sky high  standards set by the previous ladies  younger women in the audience will more  easily identify with a girl like  michelle  rather than comparing themselves to a  super model or a super genius  and feeling like they come up short  quirks and all  we choose zendaya's mj as the best  romantic lead in spider-man history  she's more than a pretty face actively  contributes to the plot  and feels the most real out of any of  the girls that have caught spider-man's  eye  what other changes were made in the  latest iteration of spider-man that you  think work well  or maybe there are new elements that you  think don't work at all  either way tell us in the comments be  sure to let us know if you want more  spider-man related videos in the future  hit that like button and subscribe
 

